                                    "widgetType": "text-editor",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "editor": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\"><a href=\"https://www.biopentra.eu/\" style=\"color:#1F5FAE;text-decoration:none\">Home</a> &gt; Resources &gt; Lyophilized Research Materials</p>",
                                        "text_color": "#3D4F66"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "lyoH1",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "heading",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "header_size": "h1",
                                        "title": "Lyophilized Research Materials",
                                        "title_color": "#0F1F33"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                },
                                {
                                    "id": "lyointro",
                                    "elType": "widget",
                                    "widgetType": "text-editor",
                                    "settings": {
                                        "editor": "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Lyophilized research materials are freeze-dried preparations used widely in laboratory settings. In simple terms, lyophilization removes moisture from a material while it is frozen, leaving a dry powder or cake that is easier to store and ship than many liquid forms.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Research suppliers often use this format for peptide stability during transport and inventory holding. Dry materials can reduce routine moisture exposure in the lab, provided they are kept cool, protected from light, and handled according to institutional protocols.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">Many peptide products in research commerce are supplied as lyophilized peptides because the format aligns with common laboratory workflows and catalog organization. This page explains the terminology, practical handling themes, and how lyophilized listings relate to other BioPentra resource guides.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#3D4F66\">The content is educational and intended for qualified laboratory research contexts only. It does not describe medical use, preparation steps for administration, or guarantees about shelf life.</p>",
                                        "text_color": "#3D4F66"
                                    },
                                    "elements": []
                                }
                            ],
                            "isInner": true
                        }
                    ],
